12:["$","div","04",{"className":"rounded-md border border-border bg-bg-muted/20 p-6 md:p-8","children":[["$","div",null,{"className":"mb-4 flex items-start gap-4","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"font-mono text-xs text-fg-muted shrink-0 mt-1","children":"04"}],["$","div",null,{"children":[["$","p",null,{"className":"mb-1 text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-wider text-accent","children":"Scope"}],["$","h3",null,{"className":"text-lg font-bold text-fg","children":"90-day timelines for problems fixable in a week"}]]}]]}],["$","p",null,{"className":"text-base text-fg-muted leading-7 mb-4","children":"A meta description that is 197 characters can be fixed in 90 seconds. A CTA that doesn't contrast against its background can be fixed in one CSS line. A headline that doesn't match the ad that sent the traffic can be rewritten in an afternoon. Agencies bundle these fixes into multi-month roadmaps because the engagement model requires it."}],["$","div",null,{"className":"border-l-2 border-accent/40 pl-4","children":["$","p",null,{"className":"text-sm text-fg-muted leading-6","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"font-semibold text-fg","children":"The alternative: "}],"The highest-priority page fixes are almost always structural and fast. Run the audit, find the highest-priority failing signal, fix it, re-audit. The whole loop runs in days, not quarters."]}]}]]}]
13:["$","div","05",{"className":"rounded-md border border-border bg-bg-muted/20 p-6 md:p-8","children":[["$","div",null,{"className":"mb-4 flex items-start gap-4","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"font-mono text-xs text-fg-muted shrink-0 mt-1","children":"05"}],["$","div",null,{"children":[["$","p",null,{"className":"mb-1 text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-wider text-accent","children":"Attribution"}],["$","h3",null,{"className":"text-lg font-bold text-fg","children":"Claiming credit for conversion lift they didn't cause"}]]}]]}],["$","p",null,{"className":"text-base text-fg-muted leading-7 mb-4","children":"If conversion rate increases during a CRO engagement, the agency takes credit. If it decreases, the issue is attributed to traffic quality or seasonality. Without a defined experiment protocol and a measurement window agreed before the fix is implemented, before/after comparisons are stories, not evidence."}],["$","div",null,{"className":"border-l-2 border-accent/40 pl-4","children":["$","p",null,{"className":"text-sm text-fg-muted leading-6","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"font-semibold text-fg","children":"The alternative: "}],"The Nebula approach: run the audit, document the failing signal and its evidence, implement the specific fix, run the audit again after a defined window, compare the signal scores. The before/after is the product, not the retainer."]}]}]]}]
